    <script type="text/javascript">
        function displayEmail() {
            var asciiEmail = '&#99;&#109;&#101;&#115;&#115;&#101;&#64;&#108;&#98;&#108;&#46;&#103;&#111;&#118;'; // Encoded email address
            var element = document.getElementById('email');
            element.innerHTML = '<a href="mailto:' + asciiEmail + '">' + asciiEmail + '</a>';
        }
    </script>
    <style>
        /* Additional styles for the flavor matrix */
        .package-table {
            border-collapse: collapse;
            width: 100%;
        }
        .package-table th {
            background-color: #f0f0f0;
            position: sticky;
            top: 0;
            z-index: 10;
        }
        .package-table td.center-check {
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 1.2em;
        }
        .flavor-header {
            writing-mode: vertical-rl;
            text-orientation: mixed;
            white-space: nowrap;
            padding: 8px 4px;
            min-width: 30px;
        }
        .package-name {
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>

<body onload="displayEmail();">
<header>
<nav>
    <a href="index.html" title="BELFEM">BELFEM</a>
    <a href="scls.html" title="SCLs">SCLS</a>
    <a href="publications.html" title="Publications">Publications</a>
    <a href="contact.html" title="Contact">Contact</a>
</nav>
</header>
<main class="container">
    <h1>Scientific Core Libraries {{ release_version }} Repository</h1>
    <table class="invisible-table" style="border: none;">
        <tr>
            <td class="left" style="border: none;">
                <img src="logo.gif" alt="SCLS Logo" style="width: 100%;">
            </td>
            <td class="right" style="border: none;">
                <p>The Scientific Core Libraries repository is a collection of open-source numerical libraries. They are meant to be used on an Intel Core or Intel Xeon <code>x86_64</code> Architecture running an Enterprise Linux system such as <a href="https://www.redhat.com/en/technologies/linux-platforms/enterprise-linux">RedHat</a>, <a href="https://rockylinux.org">Rocky</a> or <a href="https://almalinux.org">Alma</a>.</p>

                <p>The installations are kept in <code>/opt/scls/&lt;flavor&gt;</code> to not interfere with the operating system.</p>
                <p>Send comments, questions or suggestions to <b id="email">Christian Messe: [javascript protected email]</b></p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </table>

    <h3>SCLS Flavors for Enterprise Linux 9</h3>
    <ul>
        {% for group in flavor_groups %}
        <li><strong>{{ group.title }}</strong>
            <p>{{ group.description }}</p>
            <ul>
                {% for flavor in group.flavors %}
                <li><code><b>{{ flavor.name }}</b></code> - {{ flavor.description }}</li>
                {% endfor %}
            </ul>
            <br>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    <h3>Installation on Enterprise Linux 9</h3>
    <p>To install a flavor, <a href="https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/el9/x86_64/scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.el9.noarch.rpm">download the release package</a> and type this into your bash:</p>
    <code><b>sudo dnf install <a href="https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/el9/x86_64/scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.el9.noarch.rpm">scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.el9.noarch.rpm</a></b></code><br>
    <code><b>sudo dnf update</b></code><br>
    <code><b>sudo dnf install scls-&lt;flavor&gt;</b></code><br>
    <p>After installation, call the following command to set up your paths:</p>
    <code><b>source /opt/scls/&lt;flavor&gt;/bin/activate</b></code><br>
    <p>This script will add the <code>*/bin</code> directory to your path and set the <code>SCLS</code> environment variable to point to <code>/opt/scls/&lt;flavor&gt;</code></p>

    <h3>SCLS Flavor for Amazon Linux 2023</h3>
    <p>For Amazon Linux, only selected flavors are available. To install, you can type:</p>
    <code><b>sudo yum install <a href="https://belfem.lbl.gov/scls/amzn2023/x86_64/scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.amzn2023.noarch.rpm">scls-release-{{ release_version }}-1.amzn2023.noarch.rpm</a></b></code><br>
    <code><b>sudo yum update</b></code><br>
    <code><b>sudo yum install scls-&lt;flavor&gt;</b></code><br>

    <h3>Integer Indexing</h3>
    <p>All libraries within this repository are compiled with 32-bit integers, ensuring compatibility with a wide range of applications. If you require libraries with 64-bit integers, the compilation files and instructions will be provided in the GitHub repository associated with this collection.</p>

    <h3>Git Repository</h3>
    <p>If you want to build your own flavor, feel free to check out the git repository with the build recipes:<br><br>
    <code><b><a href="https://github.com/cmesse/scls">git clone https://github.com/cmesse/scls.git</a></b></code></p>

    <h3>Packages</h3>
    <table class="package-table">
        <tr class="gray-bg">
            <th>Name</th>
            <th>Version</th>
            <th>Description</th>
            {% for flavor in flavors %}
            <th class="flavor-header">{{ flavor.name }}</th>
            {% endfor %}
        </tr>
        {% for package in packages %}
        <tr {% if loop.index is odd %}class="gray-bg"{% endif %}>
            <td class="left">
                {% if package.homepage %}
                <a href="{{ package.homepage }}" class="package-name">{{ package.name }}</a>
                {% else %}
                <span class="package-name">{{ package.name }}</span>
                {% endif %}
            </td>
            <td class="center">{{ package.version }}</td>
            <td class="left">{{ package.summary }}</td>
            {% for flavor in flavors %}
            <td class="center-check">
                {% if package|package_available(flavor.name) %}
                ✓
                {% else %}
                -
                {% endif %}
            </td>
            {% endfor %}
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
    </table>
    <br>

    <h3>Known Issues</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><b>PETSc</b>
            <ul>
                <li>For the Intel compiler, compilation fails with both CUDA and OpenMP enabled. The Intel version of PETSc is compiled with either CUDA or OpenMP, not both.</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li><b>Strumpack</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Tests <code>Sparse_HOLDR_mpi_1</code> and <code>Sparse_mpi_16</code> fail</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li><b>SuiteSparse</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Experimental tests of <code>LAGraph</code> fail when using the Intel Compiler</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
        <li><b>Slate</b>
            <ul>
                <li>The tests for <code>heev</code> fail</li>
            </ul>
        </li>
    </ul>

